<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore 1996 industrial output up 3.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore 1996 industrial output up 3.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output rose 3.4 percent in 1996, compared to 10 percent in 1995, the Ministry of Trade and Industry said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The moderation in growth was partly attributed to the global electronics slowdown and the sluggish transport equipment sector.</p>
<p>The key electronics sector grew 6.7 percent in 1996 compared to 19.1 in 1995, the ministry said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom 65-8703080</p>
